# Vibe Contract — AI Hints for Replit

## Project Overview
Vibe Contract is a Replit-ready Solana smart contract factory for hackathon participants.
Users pick a template, optionally customize with AI, build, deploy, and get outputs.

## Tech Stack
- Anchor 0.31.1 (Rust) for smart contracts
- Next.js 14 + Tailwind + shadcn/ui for the frontend
- Solana devnet only

## Key Paths
- `programs/active-program/src/lib.rs` — the active smart contract
- `templates/` — six template contracts (escrow, voting, tipping, registry, coinflip, blank)
- `frontend/` — Next.js app (run with `npm run dev`)
- `scripts/build.sh` — builds the contract
- `scripts/deploy.sh` — deploys to devnet
- `deployer-keypair.json` — devnet wallet
- `output/` — build artifacts (IDL, program ID, client snippet)

## Code Style
- ALL code must be heavily commented in plain English
- Customization points marked with `// CUSTOMIZE:`
- Extension points marked with `// EXTEND:`

## Skills Reference
See `.replit-skills/` for Solana/Anchor development guides:
- `SKILL.md` — overview and operating procedure
- `programs-anchor.md` — Anchor patterns and macros
- `idl-codegen.md` — IDL and client generation
- `common-errors.md` — error diagnosis and fixes
- `compatibility-matrix.md` — version pinning
